    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2KgDpD79Y9VMv49HyVJm1LH)_\n\n**Before:** search commands were spread over many packages and keys (`consult-*`, `rg`, `deadgrep`, `org-semantic`, `p-search`, Recoll, notes grep), with no single place to start.\n\n**After:** `C-c s m` opens `sp-search-menu`, a transient popup that gathers them.\n\n## Changes (`sp-search` module and doc, CHANGELOG)\n- **Reading of \"decorated buffer like Magit\":** a transient popup with a dashboard-style header (search directory and project, which completion frameworks are active, warning if `rg` is missing). I did not build a Magit-style status buffer.\n- Groups: buffer and directory (consult-line, imenu, ripgrep, snapfile, consult-todo), grep buffers (rg, deadgrep, ag, Recoll), notes grep (`sp-search-in-notes`, `org-node-grep`, `vulpea-grep`, consult-notes), semantic (`org-semantic-*`, `p-search`, reindex), omni.\n- Every package command is guarded with `fboundp`, so nothing dead is offered. `vulpea-grep` is not defined anywhere in the config, so it shows only if a package provides it.\n- **Tab-inbox slot:** key `t` points to `sp-tab-inbox-p-search`, hidden until that command exists. No p-search PR was open or merged when I checked, so add the real name in the menu once it lands.\n- Doc `sp-search.org`: new \"The search menu\" section with a table of what each command does, and how the menu links to Vertico, vertico-posframe, Orderless, Marginalia, Embark (export to grep/occur buffers), Ivy/Counsel (Recoll only), Prescient; Corfu/Cape have no link.\n- The module already existed (`base/navi/sp-search`) so I extended it; `docs/main.org` already lists it.\n- **Key clash:** `sp-keys` rebinds `C-c s l` and `C-c s r` to easysession later, shadowing the Consult keys in `sp-search`. The menu has `l`/`r`. I used `C-c s m` because `C-c s s` is easysession save.\n\n## Not tested\nEmacs is not available in the container: parens balanced and doc/module sync checked by script only.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiDUoXY1ELdh9Lq9G8Z)_",
